                    {
                        "sense_id": "2ff7a9bc-820c-3a30-9c0a-977c392846d5",
                        "entry_id": "5b6fc134-3a98-303e-ae20-e70691fe9b02",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having two points."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa65dee8-f7aa-4fe2-8c72-2fd2daf315b4",
                                "sense_id": "2ff7a9bc-820c-3a30-9c0a-977c392846d5",
                                "text": "Finally, a study by Verhoeff indicates the possibility of the occurrence of visual apparent movement in the absence of serial bipunctual stimulation of the visual cortex."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "199b6fc7-c609-41a2-b71e-09ab3c015fbf",
                                "sense_id": "2ff7a9bc-820c-3a30-9c0a-977c392846d5",
                                "text": "We limit this paper to the bipunctual case : the signal is transmitted from a point A to a point B."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2cda3723-57b9-3f95-8532-19d2ad865750",
                        "entry_id": "5b6fc134-3a98-303e-ae20-e70691fe9b02",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relative to two distinct reference points."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7eac13e5-a949-4840-9834-ee6e181e9c78",
                                "sense_id": "2cda3723-57b9-3f95-8532-19d2ad865750",
                                "text": "The two systems are, in fact, practically identical; whatever can be proved for or with the one can be proved for or with the other; and it is only their relations to the bipunctual and bilinear systems that the distinction between the tripunctual and the trilinear systems comes into play: tripunctual coordinates standing in the same relation to bipunctual coordinates as trilinear to bilinear ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "23dd4b39-ccc5-433d-bf26-60718971a8b1",
                                "sense_id": "2cda3723-57b9-3f95-8532-19d2ad865750",
                                "text": "If X, Y, Z be a self-polar triad in regard to a conic, and O be any point, and XO, YO, and ZO meet YZ, ZX, XY, respectively, in A, B, C, then the conic is bipunctual in regard to A , B , C."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "082dd4d1-0e9c-4884-b614-c31a0a2199be",
                                "sense_id": "2cda3723-57b9-3f95-8532-19d2ad865750",
                                "text": "There are only two rectangular hyperbolas circumscribed to a given triangle and inpolar to a Bipunctual circle, namely those passing respectively through the points for which the circle is Bipunctual ."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
